    "result_text": "Inserts use explicit column lists, so the nullable new column is unaffected. The implementation is complete and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the registration-date rule for `POST /api/owners`: when the request omits `registrationDate`, it defaults to the server's current date, and it's always returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\nChanges, each kept to its natural home:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Because `Owner` extends `OwnerFields`, this makes the field both accepted on create and returned on read, and `format: date` gives the generated DTOs a `LocalDate` that Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD` (consistent with the existing `birthDate` handling).\n\n2. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added a `registrationDate` `LocalDate` field mapped to a `registration_date` column, with getter/setter. MapStruct maps it in both directions automatically by name, so `OwnerMapper` needed no changes.\n\n3. **DB schemas** \u2014 added a nullable `registration_date DATE` column to the owners table in all four dialects (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres). The test profile uses hsqldb.\n\n4. **`DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate`** \u2014 a new single-responsibility OfficeFloor function that sets `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` only when the built owner has none, wired into `owners.POST.yml` as a `defaultRegistrationDate` step between `build` and `save` (under the same `transaction` governance). A supplied date flows straight through the mapper and is left untouched.\n\nFull test suite: **2 run, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS** \u2014 both the \"defaults to today\" and \"keeps supplied date\" acceptance tests pass.",
